config INPUT_PROCESSOR_JUMP_ACCEL
    bool "Whole-vector jump-curve pointer acceleration input processor"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_POINTING
    help
      Enables a ZMK input processor implementing a RawAccel-style two-zone
      whole-vector acceleration curve for relative pointer input: a flat
      low-speed factor, a smootherstep transition, and a flat high-speed
      factor, driven by whole-vector speed (sqrt(dx^2+dy^2)/dt) rather than
      per-axis speed, with fractional remainder tracking so low factors
      don't quantize slow movement to zero.
